Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 20:35:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sandbox): contain escaped descendants in a PID namespace;
 stop tree-kill from signalling the caller's own process group
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two verified safety fixes for the handoff's unresolved escaped-descendant problem.

1. Process-ownership containment (Linux): every sandbox run now executes inside its
   own PID namespace via `unshare --user --map-root-user --pid --fork --mount-proc
   --kill-child=KILL`. Containment is kernel-enforced: when the namespace init (the
   workload root) dies for any reason, the kernel SIGKILLs all remaining members,
   including setsid escapees. PR_SET_PDEATHSIG on the wrapper tears the namespace
   down when the owning process dies. Fail closed: when the containment probe fails,
   the run errors with "[containment unavailable]" and the workload never starts.
   Windows (taskkill /T) and macOS (group kill) paths are unchanged and claim no
   escaped-descendant containment; agent-browser spawns are intentionally unwrapped
   (its persistent Chrome daemon must outlive one-shot commands).

2. posix_kill_tree root cause: strace shows procps `/bin/kill -9 -<pgid>` (without
   `--)` executes kill(0, SIGKILL) — it SIGKILLs the CALLER'S OWN PROCESS GROUP.
   That is the likely root cause of the Ubuntu CI "hosted runner lost communication"
   failures previously attributed to "infra, not code", and it killed the local test
   harness the same way. Tree-kill now calls the kill(2) syscall directly (no parser,
   no subprocess), refusing pids 0 and 1.

Tests (all visible, platform scopes kept):
- NEW escaped_setsid_descendant_does_not_survive_normal_cleanup (RED before
  containment: the escapee survives the group kill) with unrelated-process isolation.
- NEW escaped_setsid_descendant_does_not_survive_timeout_cleanup.
- NEW owner_crash_tears_down_contained_run_tree (helper process SIGKILLed; RED
  before containment: the run tree leaks).
- NEW containment_unavailable_fails_closed_without_running_workload (helper
  process; asserts the workload never executes without containment).
- NEW escaped_setsid_containment_skipped_non_linux: explicit platform-boundary
  skip marker.
- kill_pid_tree_kills_grandchild_on_posix keeps its behavioral assertion; its
  liveness probe is cmdline-marker-based on Linux because `$!` is namespace-local
  under containment (kill -0 of an ns-local pid probes the wrong host process).

Local diagnostic results (not release acceptance): 5/5 containment, 35/35 sandbox,
25/25 browser tests pass; clippy -D warnings and cargo fmt clean. Hosted acceptance
is the CI run on this exact head.

